---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WhereWeWork from '../components/WhereWeWork.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Story — Virtue Literacy Africa"
  description="Virtue Literacy Africa advances literacy for children in pastoralist, refugee, and arid and semi-arid communities across Kenya, Ethiopia, and South Sudan."
  currentPage="/about"
>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Our Story</span>
      <h1>A gap of access, not ability.</h1>
      <p>Virtue Literacy Africa is dedicated to advancing literacy for children and youth in marginalised and displaced communities across Africa, currently working in Kenya, Ethiopia, and South Sudan.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 1 — THE GAP -->
  <section class="background-section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <span class="kicker">The gap we are closing</span>
      <h2>Why the gap exists.</h2>
      <p>Our work reaches pastoralist communities, refugee populations, and children in arid and semi-arid areas. These are communities that carry deep resilience and hard-won knowledge of adapting to change, yet whose children frequently face some of the widest gaps in access to schooling and literacy support.</p>
      <p>The causes are structural rather than personal. Seasonal migration moves families before a school year ends. Displacement interrupts schooling, often more than once. Dry and unpredictable environments make attendance a question of water and distance before it is a question of willingness. And education systems, almost everywhere, are designed around populations that stay in one place.</p>
      <p>Virtue Literacy Africa works to close this gap by meeting children where they are, rather than expecting them to fit into systems that were never built for their circumstances.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 2 — HOW WE WORK -->
  <section class="background-section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <span class="kicker">How we work</span>
      <h2>Programmes that move with the community.</h2>
      <p>We work at the intersection of literacy and innovation, including artificial intelligence, to open new pathways for learning, opportunity, and voice for young people whose communities have often been overlooked by conventional systems.</p>

      <div class="ps-grid" style="margin-top:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.5rem)">
        <div>
          <h3>Rooted in the community</h3>
          <p>Community literacy programmes, mobile learning initiatives, and community reading spaces, delivered in partnership with religious institutions, families, local leaders, and the communities themselves. We build on existing trust rather than starting from scratch, and design programmes that adapt as the people we serve adapt.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Open to new tools</h3>
          <p>We are embracing innovation, including artificial intelligence, to expand access to learning and equip children and youth with tools fit for the future, without losing sight of the communities we serve. That includes early developmental screening through Mwangaza AI, in places where specialist services are otherwise out of reach.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        <span class="callout-label">Inclusion</span>
        <h3>Undetected disability is a literacy barrier.</h3>
        <p>Children who cannot hear, see, or process language are frequently mistaken for slow learners rather than identified and supported. In pastoralist, arid, and semi-arid communities, where specialists and screening services are often entirely out of reach, these children may never be identified at all.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- VISION & MISSION -->
  <section class="vm-section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">Our Foundation</span>
      <div class="vm-grid">
        <div class="vm-cell">
          <span class="vm-label">Vision</span>
          <h3>A future where every child, regardless of geography, mobility, or circumstance, has the literacy skills and tools to shape their own opportunity and voice.</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="vm-cell">
          <span class="vm-label">Mission</span>
          <p>To advance literacy for children and youth in marginalised and displaced communities across Africa, including pastoralist populations, refugee communities, and children in arid and semi-arid areas, by combining community-rooted programmes, research and evidence-sharing, and innovation, including artificial intelligence.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- VALUES -->
  <section class="beneficiaries-section reveal">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">What guides us</span>
      <h2>Our values.</h2>
      <ul class="beneficiaries">
        <li>
          <span class="bn">01</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Dignity</h4>
            <p>Every child deserves to be seen, valued, and given a genuine chance to learn, regardless of where or how they live.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">02</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Community</h4>
            <p>We walk alongside families, local leaders, and institutions like churches, building on existing trust rather than starting from scratch.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">03</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Resilience</h4>
            <p>We draw inspiration from the communities we serve, who have long adapted to change, and we design programmes that adapt with them.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">04</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Innovation</h4>
            <p>We embrace new tools, including artificial intelligence, to expand what is possible in literacy and learning without losing sight of culture and context.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="bn">05</span>
          <div class="btext">
            <h4>Access</h4>
            <p>We meet children where they are, removing barriers created by distance, mobility, and systems not built with them in mind.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHERE WE WORK -->
  <WhereWeWork
    kicker="Where we work"
    heading="Reaching pastoralist, refugee, and drylands communities across East Africa."
  />

  <!-- SECTION 4 — WHAT WE ARE BUILDING -->
  <section class="background-section">
    <div class="container reveal">
      <span class="kicker">What we are building</span>
      <h2>Literacy is more than a skill.</h2>
      <p>It is a foundation for dignity, opportunity, and voice. We are committed to walking alongside marginalised and displaced communities in Kenya, Ethiopia, and South Sudan, using both tradition and innovation, to make that foundation accessible to every child.</p>
      <p>That work runs across five pillars, from the literacy programmes that reach a child in a mobile community to the evidence we put in front of the people deciding how those communities are served.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.25rem)"><a href="/team" class="btn">Meet the team &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="act">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Be part of it.</h2>
      <div class="act-grid reveal">
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Partner with us</h3>
          <p>Financial sponsors, in-kind donors, faith institutions, and development partners.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/get-involved">See how to get involved &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Read our findings</h3>
          <p>Reports and briefs on what works in literacy, inclusive education, and AI-enabled learning.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/research">Research &amp; findings &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="act-cell">
          <h3>Contact us</h3>
          <p>Questions, media enquiries, or an opening conversation about what we are building.</p>
          <a class="go" href="/contact">Get in touch &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
